  "problem_statement": "feat(personas): custom subagent personas (.wells/agents/*.md)\n\nNew wells.personas module mirrors skills.py's discovery/caching/CRUD\npattern exactly: agents/<name>/PERSONA.md (name + description + tools\n+ system prompt), discovered from the workspace agents/ dir + optional\nWELLS_AGENTS_PATHS. Even cheaper than skills -- a persona's system\nprompt only ever reaches the SUBAGENT it's assigned to, never the\nparent's context; the parent only sees the name+description index\n(injected via personas.inject_into_prompt, guarded on background\nagents being enabled).\n\nWired into bg_start(persona=<name>, ...): subagents.persona_subagent()\nuses the persona's system_prompt as system_prefix, with role\n(research/fix/worktree) still capping the toolset for safety --\nrole=research always forces readonly regardless of what a persona's\ntools: front-matter requests. Verified live: a test persona's system\nprompt genuinely drove a real subagent's exact output.\n\n/agents CLI command (list/show/add/edit/remove) + AgentsScreen/\nAgentEditScreen TUI modal, both mirroring /skills' existing UX\none-for-one so this is immediately familiar. New WELLS_AGENTS /config\ntoggle alongside the other capability switches.\n\n(Named agents.py originally, but src/wells/agents/ already exists as\nthe planner/architect/coder/tester/reviewer package -- renamed to\npersonas.py to avoid the collision.)",
